Bundled SuiteSparse for ngspice
===============================

This directory holds an unmodified copy of the parts of SuiteSparse that
the KLU sparse solver needs:

  SuiteSparse 7.14.1 (Sept 12, 2026)
  KLU 2.3.6, AMD 3.3.4, BTF 2.3.3, COLAMD 3.3.5, SuiteSparse_config

  https://github.com/DrTimothyAldenDavis/SuiteSparse
  KLU, BTF: LGPL-2.1-or-later    AMD, COLAMD, SuiteSparse_config: BSD-3-Clause
  (see License_*.txt)

It is used only if configure (or CMake) finds no installed SuiteSparse KLU,
or if ngspice is configured with --with-suitesparse=no
(CMake: -DNGSPICE_KLU_PROVIDER=bundled).

KLU, AMD, BTF and COLAMD need neither BLAS nor LAPACK.

Only the 32 bit integer routines are built.  The complex KLU routines
(klu_z_*) are made by compiling the numeric sources a second time with
-DCOMPLEX, exactly as SuiteSparse does in its klu_z_*.c wrapper files.

ngspice specific code is not in this directory:

  src/include/ngspice/klu.h      selects bundled or installed KLU
  src/include/ngspice/klu_ext.h  ngspice additions to the KLU API
  src/maths/KLU/klusmp.c         SMP interface of ngspice
  src/maths/KLU/klu_utils.c      klu_extract_Udiag, klu_print, CSR conversion
  src/maths/KLU/klu_multiply.c   matrix-vector and constant multiplication
  src/maths/KLU/klu_compat.c     KLU_EMPTY_MATRIX handling for n == 0
  src/maths/KLU/klu_ngspice.h    private header of the files above

Until SuiteSparse 3.7.0 (KLU 1.1.3) the bundled sources were modified for
ngspice.  These changes are now outside of this directory:

  - KLU_EMPTY_MATRIX for a matrix of dimension 0       -> klu_compat.c
  - klu_extract_Udiag, klu_print                       -> klu_utils.c
  - memgrow = initmem_amd = 10 in klu_defaults()       -> klusmp.c
  - lsolve_symbolic and construct_column merged in
    klu_kernel.c (a speed optimisation)                -> dropped, no
                                                          measurable gain

Update
------

  1. ./import.sh /path/to/SuiteSparse
  2. update the version numbers above
  3. if files were added or removed in SuiteSparse: adapt import.sh and
     Makefile.am here, then run  python3 cmake/am2cmake.py
  4. rebuild with --with-suitesparse=no and run the tests with KLU, e.g.

       mkdir -p /tmp/kluhome && echo "option klu" > /tmp/kluhome/.spiceinit
       HOME=/tmp/kluhome make check

     ngspice uses Sparse 1.3 by default, so without "option klu" the
     tests do not exercise KLU.
